-- title:
--   Addition is continuous on the elementary Schwartz–Bruhat space
-- statement:
--   Let $E=\mathbb R^m\times\mathbb T^n\times\mathbb Z^r\times F$ be an elementary abelian Lie group and let $\mathcal S(E)$ be its Schwartz–Bruhat space with the topology of Definition D.1.3.1. That topology is generated by the seminorms
--   $$\nu_{i,j,k}(g)=\sup|a|^j|x|^i\,\|D^kg_{a,b}(x,t)\|,$$
--   and is formalized as the topology induced by the map $g\mapsto(D^k\text{-weighted derivatives})$ into a product of spaces of uniformly convergent functions. Then addition $\mathcal S(E)\times\mathcal S(E)\to\mathcal S(E)$ is continuous. The reason is that the inducing map is additive: every element of $\mathcal S(E)$ is smooth, so $D^k(g+h)=D^kg+D^kh$, and its target is a topological additive group.
-- source:
--   A. M. Masullo, The Music of the Primes, draft of 20 November 2026, https://math216.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/the-music-of-the-primes.pdf, Appendix D, Definition D.1.3.1

import Definitions.Def_MasulloGRH_SchwartzBruhat

set_option autoImplicit false

namespace MasulloGRH

theorem elemSchwartz_continuousAdd {m n r s : ℕ} {d : Fin s → ℕ} :
    ContinuousAdd (ElemSchwartz m n r s d) := by
  sorry

end MasulloGRH
